discussion_comments.comment_body:
Not quite - LoadContext is used for any variable that is both a) accessed in a function expression and b) reassigned somewhere. So it can also be used for things like:

```
function Component()
  function OnClick(e) {
    let value = null; // context variable 
    if (e.target) {
      value = e.target.value
    }
  }
}
``` 


You’ll need to check against the function expression’s context. It’s an easy mistake to make, I did the other day. See https://github.com/facebook/react/pull/34904 for checking against the function’s context.

